# The auto-configurations @LudwigRestClientTest boots. Deliberately the whole starter and nothing
# else: a slice that left out, say, the auth auto-configuration would pass tests that production
# fails, which is worse than having no slice.
#
# audit-core's auto-configuration is here for the same reason: this starter's AuditRecorder needs an
# AuditSink, so a slice without it would fail to start rather than run the tests it exists for. It
# brings the SLF4J sink alone - no database, no scheduler, no broker.
org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.jackson.JacksonAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.restclient.config.RestClientAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.restclient.config.RestClientAuthAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.restclient.config.RestClientObservabilityAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.restclient.config.RestClientInterfaceAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.restclient.config.RestClientWebCoreAutoConfiguration
ru.ludwigandreas.audit.config.AuditCoreAutoConfiguration
